{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"ir-remote","name":"IR remote and receiver","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"The little 21-key infrared remote and an IR receiver module (VS1838B). Press the remote's keys in the run panel; every receiver on the bench picks up the code (NEC protocol). Includes IRremote.h, both its new (IrReceiver) and old (IRrecv) ways.","category":"Wireless","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// Infrared: the remote flashes a code (NEC: address, its inverse, command, its inverse) and every\n// receiver that can see it turns the flashes into its signal pin. Here the remote puts its codes in\n// the room (shared by the parts of this library) and each receiver sends them down its S wire.\n\nconst KEYS = { 'CH-': 0x45, CH: 0x46, 'CH+': 0x47, '|<<': 0x44, '>>|': 0x40, '>||': 0x43, '-': 0x07, '+': 0x15, EQ: 0x09, '0': 0x16, '100+': 0x19, '200+': 0x0d, '1': 0x0c, '2': 0x18, '3': 0x5e, '4': 0x08, '5': 0x1c, '6': 0x5a, '7': 0x42, '8': 0x52, '9': 0x4a };\nconst room = []; // [{ time, data }] codes in the air (a held key repeats: data [] = \"still held\")\n\nbench.device('ir-remote', (part) => {\n  const keys = part.control('keys');\n  const screen = part.screen('keys');\n  const order = ['CH-', 'CH', 'CH+', '|<<', '>>|', '>||', '-', '+', 'EQ', '0', '100+', '200+', '1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6', '7', '8', '9'];\n  let held = null, nextRepeat = 0, sent = 0, last = '';\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      for (const k of keys.take()) {\n        const cmd = KEYS[k];\n        if (cmd === undefined) continue;\n        room.push({ time: io.time, data: [0x00, 0xff, cmd, (~cmd) & 255] });\n        held = k;\n        last = `${k} (0x${cmd.toString(16).toUpperCase().padStart(2, '0')})`;\n        nextRepeat = io.time + 0.108; // NEC: a repeat code every 108 ms while held\n        sent++;\n      }\n      const down = keys.down;\n      if (held && !down.includes(held)) held = null;\n      if (held && io.time >= nextRepeat) {\n        room.push({ time: io.time, data: [] });\n        nextRepeat += 0.108;\n      }\n      while (room.length && room[0].time < io.time - 1) room.shift();\n      order.forEach((k, i) => screen.set(i % 3, Math.floor(i / 3), down.includes(k) ? 1 : 0));\n    },\n    status() { return [sent ? `sent ${sent} codes, the last ${last}` : 'press its keys in the run panel']; },\n  };\n});\n\nbench.device('ir-receiver', (part) => {\n  let seen = -1, powered = false, got = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      const v = io.supply('+', '-');\n      powered = v >= 2.7;\n      if (!powered) { io.release('S'); return; }\n      io.drive('S', v, 1); // its output rests high\n      for (const c of room) {\n        if (c.time <= seen) continue;\n        io.send('S', 'ir', c.data);\n        if (c.data.length) got++;\n      }\n      if (room.length) seen = room[room.length - 1].time;\n      io.draw(0.0015);\n    },\n    status() { return [powered ? `${got} codes received` : 'no power (+ needs 3.3-5 V)']; },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"IRremote.h":{"classes":["IRrecv","decode_results"],"exports":["IrReceiver","ENABLE_LED_FEEDBACK","DISABLE_LED_FEEDBACK","USE_DEFAULT_FEEDBACK_LED_PIN","IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT","NEC","UNKNOWN"],"code":"// IRremote (Armin Joachimsmeyer & co), NEC codes, both ways sketches use it:\n//   new: IrReceiver.begin(pin, ENABLE_LED_FEEDBACK); if (IrReceiver.decode()) { IrReceiver.decodedIRData.command;\n//        IrReceiver.printIRResultShort(&Serial); IrReceiver.resume(); }\n//   old: IRrecv irrecv(pin); decode_results results; irrecv.enableIRIn(); if (irrecv.decode(&results)) { results.value; irrecv.resume(); }\nconst ENABLE_LED_FEEDBACK = true, DISABLE_LED_FEEDBACK = false, USE_DEFAULT_FEEDBACK_LED_PIN = 0;\nconst IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT = 0x01;\nconst UNKNOWN = 0, NEC = 8;\nconst hex = (n, w = 2) => '0x' + (n >>> 0).toString(16).toUpperCase().padStart(w, '0');\nconst rev8 = (b) => { let r = 0; for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) r |= ((b >> i) & 1) << (7 - i); return r; };\n\nclass IRReceiverClass {\n  constructor() {\n    this.pin = -1;\n    this.queue = [];\n    this.lastCode = null;\n    this.decodedIRData = { protocol: UNKNOWN, address: 0, command: 0, flags: 0, decodedRawData: 0, numberOfBits: 0 };\n  }\n  begin(pin, feedback = false) {\n    this.pin = pin;\n    pinMode(pin, INPUT);\n    if (feedback && typeof LED_BUILTIN === 'number') pinMode(LED_BUILTIN, OUTPUT);\n    this.feedback = !!feedback && typeof LED_BUILTIN === 'number';\n  }\n  start() {}\n  stop() {}\n  enableIRIn() {}\n  available() { this.pull(); return this.queue.length > 0; }\n  pull() {\n    if (this.pin < 0) return;\n    for (const m of linkReceive(this.pin, 'ir')) this.queue.push(m.data);\n    if (this.queue.length > 16) this.queue.splice(0, this.queue.length - 16);\n  }\n  /** a code arrived? its address and command are in decodedIRData */\n  decode() {\n    this.pull();\n    if (!this.queue.length) return false;\n    const d = this.queue.shift();\n    if (this.feedback) { digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, HIGH); }\n    if (!d.length) {\n      // a repeat (the key is still held): the last code again, flagged\n      if (!this.lastCode) return false;\n      this.decodedIRData = { ...this.decodedIRData, flags: IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT };\n      return true;\n    }\n    const [addr, naddr, cmd] = d;\n    const address = ((naddr ^ 0xff) === addr) ? addr : addr | (naddr << 8);\n    this.lastCode = d;\n    this.decodedIRData = {\n      protocol: NEC, address, command: cmd, flags: 0, numberOfBits: 32,\n      decodedRawData: ((d[3] << 24) | (d[2] << 16) | (d[1] << 8) | d[0]) >>> 0,\n    };\n    return true;\n  }\n  resume() { if (this.feedback) digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, LOW); }\n  printIRResultShort(out) {\n    const d = this.decodedIRData;\n    out.println(`Protocol=${d.protocol === NEC ? 'NEC' : 'UNKNOWN'} Address=${hex(d.address)} Command=${hex(d.command)}${d.flags & IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT ? ' Repeat' : ` Raw-Data=${hex(d.decodedRawData, 8)} 32 bits LSB first`}`);\n  }\n  printIRSendUsage() {}\n}\nconst IrReceiver = new IRReceiverClass();\n\n/** the old way: results.value is the 32 bits MSB first (0xFFA25D for CH-), 0xFFFFFFFF for a repeat */\nclass decode_results {\n  constructor() { this.value = 0; this.bits = 0; this.decode_type = UNKNOWN; this.address = 0; this.command = 0; }\n}\nclass IRrecv {\n  constructor(pin) { this.r = new IRReceiverClass(); this.pin = pin; }\n  enableIRIn() { this.r.begin(this.pin); }\n  begin(pin = this.pin) { this.r.begin(pin); }\n  decode(results) {\n    if (!this.r.decode()) return false;\n    const d = this.r.decodedIRData;\n    if (results) {\n      results.decode_type = NEC;\n      results.bits = 32;\n      results.address = d.address;\n      results.command = d.command;\n      if (d.flags & IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT) results.value = 0xffffffff;\n      else {\n        const raw = d.decodedRawData;\n        results.value = ((rev8(raw & 255) << 24) | (rev8((raw >> 8) & 255) << 16) | (rev8((raw >> 16) & 255) << 8) | rev8((raw >>> 24) & 255)) >>> 0;\n      }\n    }\n    return true;\n  }\n  resume() { this.r.resume(); }\n}\n"},"IRremote.hpp":{"classes":["IRrecv","decode_results"],"exports":["IrReceiver","ENABLE_LED_FEEDBACK","DISABLE_LED_FEEDBACK","USE_DEFAULT_FEEDBACK_LED_PIN","IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT","NEC","UNKNOWN"],"code":"// IRremote (Armin Joachimsmeyer & co), NEC codes, both ways sketches use it:\n//   new: IrReceiver.begin(pin, ENABLE_LED_FEEDBACK); if (IrReceiver.decode()) { IrReceiver.decodedIRData.command;\n//        IrReceiver.printIRResultShort(&Serial); IrReceiver.resume(); }\n//   old: IRrecv irrecv(pin); decode_results results; irrecv.enableIRIn(); if (irrecv.decode(&results)) { results.value; irrecv.resume(); }\nconst ENABLE_LED_FEEDBACK = true, DISABLE_LED_FEEDBACK = false, USE_DEFAULT_FEEDBACK_LED_PIN = 0;\nconst IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT = 0x01;\nconst UNKNOWN = 0, NEC = 8;\nconst hex = (n, w = 2) => '0x' + (n >>> 0).toString(16).toUpperCase().padStart(w, '0');\nconst rev8 = (b) => { let r = 0; for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) r |= ((b >> i) & 1) << (7 - i); return r; };\n\nclass IRReceiverClass {\n  constructor() {\n    this.pin = -1;\n    this.queue = [];\n    this.lastCode = null;\n    this.decodedIRData = { protocol: UNKNOWN, address: 0, command: 0, flags: 0, decodedRawData: 0, numberOfBits: 0 };\n  }\n  begin(pin, feedback = false) {\n    this.pin = pin;\n    pinMode(pin, INPUT);\n    if (feedback && typeof LED_BUILTIN === 'number') pinMode(LED_BUILTIN, OUTPUT);\n    this.feedback = !!feedback && typeof LED_BUILTIN === 'number';\n  }\n  start() {}\n  stop() {}\n  enableIRIn() {}\n  available() { this.pull(); return this.queue.length > 0; }\n  pull() {\n    if (this.pin < 0) return;\n    for (const m of linkReceive(this.pin, 'ir')) this.queue.push(m.data);\n    if (this.queue.length > 16) this.queue.splice(0, this.queue.length - 16);\n  }\n  /** a code arrived? its address and command are in decodedIRData */\n  decode() {\n    this.pull();\n    if (!this.queue.length) return false;\n    const d = this.queue.shift();\n    if (this.feedback) { digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, HIGH); }\n    if (!d.length) {\n      // a repeat (the key is still held): the last code again, flagged\n      if (!this.lastCode) return false;\n      this.decodedIRData = { ...this.decodedIRData, flags: IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT };\n      return true;\n    }\n    const [addr, naddr, cmd] = d;\n    const address = ((naddr ^ 0xff) === addr) ? addr : addr | (naddr << 8);\n    this.lastCode = d;\n    this.decodedIRData = {\n      protocol: NEC, address, command: cmd, flags: 0, numberOfBits: 32,\n      decodedRawData: ((d[3] << 24) | (d[2] << 16) | (d[1] << 8) | d[0]) >>> 0,\n    };\n    return true;\n  }\n  resume() { if (this.feedback) digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, LOW); }\n  printIRResultShort(out) {\n    const d = this.decodedIRData;\n    out.println(`Protocol=${d.protocol === NEC ? 'NEC' : 'UNKNOWN'} Address=${hex(d.address)} Command=${hex(d.command)}${d.flags & IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT ? ' Repeat' : ` Raw-Data=${hex(d.decodedRawData, 8)} 32 bits LSB first`}`);\n  }\n  printIRSendUsage() {}\n}\nconst IrReceiver = new IRReceiverClass();\n\n/** the old way: results.value is the 32 bits MSB first (0xFFA25D for CH-), 0xFFFFFFFF for a repeat */\nclass decode_results {\n  constructor() { this.value = 0; this.bits = 0; this.decode_type = UNKNOWN; this.address = 0; this.command = 0; }\n}\nclass IRrecv {\n  constructor(pin) { this.r = new IRReceiverClass(); this.pin = pin; }\n  enableIRIn() { this.r.begin(this.pin); }\n  begin(pin = this.pin) { this.r.begin(pin); }\n  decode(results) {\n    if (!this.r.decode()) return false;\n    const d = this.r.decodedIRData;\n    if (results) {\n      results.decode_type = NEC;\n      results.bits = 32;\n      results.address = d.address;\n      results.command = d.command;\n      if (d.flags & IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT) results.value = 0xffffffff;\n      else {\n        const raw = d.decodedRawData;\n        results.value = ((rev8(raw & 255) << 24) | (rev8((raw >> 8) & 255) << 16) | (rev8((raw >> 16) & 255) << 8) | rev8((raw >>> 24) & 255)) >>> 0;\n      }\n    }\n    return true;\n  }\n  resume() { this.r.resume(); }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"receiver","name":"IR receiver (VS1838B)","description":"Picks up infrared remotes. S (signal) to a pin, + to 3.3-5 V, - to GND. Its signal rests high and carries the remote's code (NEC: an address and a command). IrReceiver.begin(PIN); ... if (IrReceiver.decode()) { IrReceiver.decodedIRData.command ... IrReceiver.resume(); }","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[1.6,0.16,2],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"box":[0.6,0.7,0.55],"at":[0,0.51,0.5],"color":"#141416"},{"sphere":0.28,"at":[0,0.75,0.78],"color":"#26262a"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["S","+","-"],"at":[-0.254,0,-0.8],"kinds":{"S":"out","+":"vin","-":"gnd"},"extra":{"+":{"label":"+ (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2.7,"vmax":5.5},"S":{"label":"S (signal)"}}}],"device":"ir-receiver"},{"id":"remote","name":"IR remote (21 keys)","description":"The small \"Car MP3\" remote with its own coin cell. Press its keys in the run panel: every IR receiver on the bench gets the code. Address 0x00; commands: CH- 0x45, CH 0x46, CH+ 0x47, |<< 0x44, >>| 0x40, >|| 0x43, - 0x07, + 0x15, EQ 0x09, 0 0x16, 100+ 0x19, 200+ 0x0D, 1 0x0C, 2 0x18, 3 0x5E, 4 0x08, 5 0x1C, 6 0x5A, 7 0x42, 8 0x52, 9 0x4A.","swatch":"#141416","mass":20,"shape":[{"box":[4,0.6,8.6],"at":[0,0.3,0],"color":"#141416"},{"screen":{"id":"keys","size":[3.4,7.4],"px":[3,7],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff5040","off":"#c9ccd2","bg":"#141416"},"at":[0,0.61,-0.3]},{"box":[0.6,0.3,0.3],"at":[0,0.3,4.4],"color":"#2a1a14","collide":false}],"controls":[{"id":"keys","kind":"keys","label":"Remote","cols":3,"keys":["CH-","CH","CH+","|<<",">>|",">||","-","+","EQ","0","100+","200+","1","2","3","4","5","6","7","8","9"]}],"device":"ir-remote"}],"examples":[{"name":"Remote control an LED","description":"Press 1 on the remote (its card in the run panel) to switch the LED on, 0 to switch it off; every key's code is printed in the serial monitor.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Remote control an LED","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-6,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"ir","type":"ir-remote/receiver","name":"IR receiver","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[4,0,-2],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"remote","type":"ir-remote/remote","name":"Remote","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[16,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"led","type":"led","name":"LED","params":{"color":"red"},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,6],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP11"},"b":{"uid":"ir","pin":"S"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"ir","pin":"+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"ir","pin":"-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"led","pin":"A"},"color":"#f08c2a"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"led","pin":"K"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Press keys on the remote (its card in the run panel): 1 = LED on, 0 = LED off.\n#include <IRremote.h>\n\n#define IR_PIN 11\n#define LED 15\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(LED, OUTPUT);\n  IrReceiver.begin(IR_PIN, ENABLE_LED_FEEDBACK);\n  Serial.println(\"Ready for the remote\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  if (IrReceiver.decode()) {\n    IrReceiver.printIRResultShort(&Serial);\n    if (!(IrReceiver.decodedIRData.flags & IRDATA_FLAGS_IS_REPEAT)) {\n      int cmd = IrReceiver.decodedIRData.command;\n      if (cmd == 0x0C) digitalWrite(LED, HIGH);   // key 1\n      if (cmd == 0x16) digitalWrite(LED, LOW);    // key 0\n    }\n    IrReceiver.resume();\n  }\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}